- Story & Context: Old Mak Mah, usually stoic, confesses to Anak Genta that the market master's latest threat, a crudely drawn eviction notice, has finally pushed her past boiling point; her trembling hands now wield not just fruit, but a determination harder than any river stone. "My heart beats with the rhythm of this anger, child."
